Z||000000||Patrick86GT||08-28-2001||05:34 PM||||Not loud but audible, I can hear a single "clunk" each time the AC clutch engages. The clunk disappears during compressor activation. Air is "cold" and there are no other apparent problems w/ function. System is R-134a converted and has been working w/o flaw since an early summer recharge.<P>My hearing isn't good, but it almost sounds like a residential water pipe air knock...as opposed to a metallic sound. <P>Could there be air in the lines causing this? <P>TX<BR>Pat   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cozmo||08-28-2001||07:28 PM||||Maybe something (line, compressor etc) is loose and banging around...<BR>Start it up, get the compressor cycling and listen through a 3' piece of garden hose to isolate where the sound is coming from. (be careful around the pullys!)<BR>At least that'll give you a starting point....<BR>Good Luck!<P>BobC||||reg||1
